        "Wudu is the spiritual and physical purification required before standing in prayer.\n\nThe Quran establishes four obligatory pillars (Fara'id) in Surah Al-Ma'idah (5:6):\n1. Washing the face from forehead to chin and ear to ear.\n2. Washing both arms including the elbows.\n3. Wiping at least a quarter of the head with wet hands (Hanafi; Sunnat is wiping the whole head).\n4. Washing both feet up to and including the ankles.\n\nProphetic Sunnahs (Recommended Practices):\n- Starting with Bismillah and intention (Niyyah) in the heart.\n- Washing the hands thrice up to wrists.\n- Rinsing the mouth (Madmadah) and cleaning the nose (Istinshaq) thrice.\n- Running wet fingers through the beard and between fingers and toes (Takhlil).\n- Maintaining sequential order (Tartib) without prolonged interruption (Muwalat)." to "Wudhu ni utakaso wa kiroho na kimwili unaohitajika kabla ya kusimama katika sala.\n\nQuran imeweka nguzo nne za lazima (Fara'id) katika Surah Al-Ma'idah (5: 6):\n1. Kuosha uso kutoka paji la uso hadi kidevu na sikio hadi sikio.\n2. Kuosha mikono yote miwili pamoja na viwiko.\n3. Kupangusa angalau robo ya kichwa kwa mikono iliyolowa maji (Hanafi; Sunnat ni kupangusa kichwa kizima).\n4. Kuosha miguu yote miwili hadi na kujumuisha vifundo vya miguu.\n\nSunnah za Kinabii (Vitendo Vinavyopendekezwa):\n- Kuanzia Bismillah na nia (Niyyah) katika moyo.\n- Kuosha mikono mara tatu hadi kwenye mikono.\n- Kusafisha mdomo (Madmadah) na kusafisha pua (Istinshaq) mara tatu.\n- Kupitisha vidole vya maji kwenye ndevu na kati ya vidole na vidole vya miguu (Takhlil).\n- Kudumisha mpangilio wa mpangilio (Tartib) bila usumbufu wa muda mrefu (Muwalat).",
        "Khushu' is inner humility, stillness of the limbs, and attentive contemplation of what one is reciting.\n\nPractical Anchors for Khushu':\n- Prepare before the Takbir: Perform wudu mindfully, arrive before iqamah, and eliminate immediate physical distractions.\n- Contemplate the Words: Recite slowly (Tartil). When saying 'Al-Hamdu lillahi Rabbil-Alameen', remember Allah responds directly: 'My servant has praised Me' (Sahih Muslim 395).\n- Fix the Gaze: Direct your gaze respectfully at the place of prostration (Sujud), rather than looking around.\n- Remember the Final Prayer: The Prophet (peace be upon him) advised: 'Pray as if it were your farewell prayer' (Sunan Ibn Majah 4171)." to "Khushu' ni unyenyekevu wa ndani, utulivu wa viungo, na kutafakari kwa makini kile mtu anachokisoma.\n\nNanga Vitendo kwa Khushu':\n- Jitayarishe kabla ya Takbir: Toa wudhu kwa uangalifu, fika kabla ya iqamah, na uondoe usumbufu wa kimwili mara moja.\n- Tafakari Maneno: Soma polepole (Tartil). Unaposema 'Al-Hamdu lillahi Rabbil-Alamiyn', kumbuka Mwenyezi Mungu anajibu moja kwa moja: 'Mja wangu amenisifu' (Sahih Muslim 395).\n- Rekebisha Macho: Elekeza macho yako kwa heshima mahali pa kusujudu (Sujud), badala ya kutazama huku na huku.\n- Kumbuka Swalah ya Mwisho: Mtume (saw) alinasihi: 'Sali kana kwamba ni sala yako ya kuaga' (Sunan Ibn Majah 4171).",
        "The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: 'Jibril kept enjoining good treatment of the neighbor upon me until I thought he would assign him a share of inheritance.' (Sahih al-Bukhari 6014).\n\nIslamic teachings identify three classes of neighbors:\n1. A neighbor who is a relative and Muslim: has three rights (kinship, Islam, neighborhood).\n2. A neighbor who is Muslim: has two rights (Islam and neighborhood).\n3. A neighbor of different faith: has the sacred right of good neighborhood and kindness.\n\nHarm to neighbors is strictly condemned: 'By Allah he does not believe... whose neighbor is not safe from his harm.' (Sahih al-Bukhari 6016)." to "Mtume Muhammad (Swalla Allaahu 'alayhi wa aalihi wa sallam) amesema: 'Jibril alikuwa akiniamrisha kumtendea mema jirani yangu mpaka nikafikiri atamgawia sehemu ya urithi.' (Swahiyh al-Bukhari 6014).\n\nMafundisho ya Kiislamu yanabainisha tabaka tatu za majirani:\n1. Jirani ambaye ni jamaa na Mwislamu: ana haki tatu (jamaa, Uislamu, ujirani).\n2. Jirani ambaye ni Muislamu: ana haki mbili (Uislamu na ujirani).\n3. Jirani wa imani tofauti: ana haki takatifu ya ujirani mwema na wema.\n\nMadhara kwa majirani yanalaaniwa vikali: 'Wallahi haamini... ambaye jirani yake hajasalimika na madhara yake.' (Swahiyh al-Bukhari 6016).",
